{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774289700,"nonce":"bZI3l4LgejofHt/zgZg0Zt6cFks=","title":"Inbox delivers already-completed/dismissed auth results","message":"Auth results that have already been completed or dismissed should not be delivered to new sessions. On 2026-03-23, a session received 21 stale auth results — all in a completed or dismissed terminal state, from various feature branches across repos.\n\n**Problem:**\nThe inbox delivery mechanism does not filter out auth results that are already in a terminal state (completed, dismissed, merged). When a new session starts, the session-start hook queries the inbox and receives these stale items, processes them, and acks them — wasting processing time and cluttering the session start with irrelevant noise.\n\n**Impact:**\n- Session startup is cluttered with 21+ stale items requiring processing\n- Agents waste time acknowledging items that have no actionable content\n- Potentially confusing if an agent misinterprets a stale \"completed\" result as belonging to a current branch\n\n**Expected behavior:**\nThe inbox delivery endpoint (or the server-side query that populates inbox items) should filter out auth results whose status is already in a terminal state (e.g., `completed`, `dismissed`, `merged`, `cancelled`) before delivering them to new sessions. Only pending or freshly-resolved results that have not yet been acknowledged by the originating session should appear.\n\n**Proposed fix:**\nIn the inbox query (likely `GET /api/inbox` or the session-start hook logic), add a filter: exclude auth_result inbox items where the corresponding auth request is already in a terminal state AND was resolved before this session started. Alternatively, at ingestion time when an auth request reaches a terminal state, purge or expire any existing unacknowledged inbox items for it rather than leaving them to accumulate.","files":null}]}